      "side": 1,
      "message": "bmcweb already had meson options to define the socket type (http/https/both) and an authentication level per socket (auth/noauth), but noauth was never actually implemented/enforced — it was accepted as configuration but had no effect. This MR implements that enforcement.\n\nThis is needed for cases where you want multiple socket types on the same bmcweb instance — for example, one HTTPS socket with authentication enabled, and a second HTTP socket with no authentication (e.g. for a trusted local/management network).",
